  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"215\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/74cc94a7-7f33-46ce-9c5c-7d9fc393bb43-image.png\" width=\"200\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constant (isothermal expansion)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math>. The graph will be a straight line, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>.&nbsp;So, the above graph is correct.<br /><br /><img height=\"207\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a830584d-bc91-420d-a154-b8aa6b58f283-image.png\" width=\"231\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constant (isothermal expansion)<br /><br />On increasing or decreasing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi></math> becomes constant. So, the above graph is correct.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;graphs are correct.<br /><br /><img height=\"221\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5566a1d1-575a-4f97-926b-1e87085bb549-image.png\" width=\"198\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constant (isothermal expansion)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math>. The graph will be a straight line,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>. So, the above graph is incorrect.<br /><br /><img height=\"220\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aa0f0fa8-4cc9-4c78-b986-88cf84356401-image.png\" width=\"195\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>nC</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mi>dT</mi></math><br /><br />and for isothermal process,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> So, the above graph is incorrect.<br /><br />Options <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> are incorrect.</p>",
